# Chroma library, modern Earth: FAR-OFF MOMENTS THROUGH TIES (item 17 "far-off events", v22.3, switch far_ties, off).
# Something happened in the town where a close tie lives (another town), and the tie reaches out: a call, a visit, a
# letter. The Engine fills the tie in the first who: slot, {their_town} with the tie's town and {far_event} with a short
# past-tense phrase for what happened; cast_want: far_hard / far_good / far_mixed and touch: pick the moment for the
# event's side and what it touched (chroma-ideas/far-off-events.md F2 to F5; sides from chroma-world/spheres/data/
# far_sides.json). Emren 2026-10-10 06:55 UTC: far-off events are multi-sided, good and mixed as well as hard, balanced
# within realism. So 12 hard, 12 good, 12 mixed here (every touch has a mixed pair). "took them in" (F4) brings the tie into the home for about a year;
# "moved away | moves: yes" (F3) takes up an offer in the tie's town. Held back while far_ties is off; no share:, gap 3-8.
# Syntax: header of build.py. Rules: library-spec.md. Everyday pairs: one calls two colors, its partner the other three,
# with matching stages, age, tone, cast_want, touch and who:; each cross cycle s1 to s4 nine times over the 36 moments.
#   pair 1  work, hard, sibling      1a BR / 1b WUG        pair 8  health, good, sibling     8a UG / 8b WBR
#   pair 2  work, good, friend       2a WU / 2b BRG        pair 9  safety, hard, sibling     9a WR / 9b UBG
#   pair 3  money, hard, parent      3a UB / 3b WRG        pair 10 safety, good, child      10a BG / 10b WUR
#   pair 4  money, good, sibling     4a RG / 4b WUB        pair 11 standing, hard, friend   11a WR / 11b UBG
#   pair 5  home, hard, parent       5a WG / 5b UBR        pair 12 standing, good, child    12a UB / 12b WRG
#   pair 6  home, good, friend       6a UR / 6b WBG        pair 13 work, mixed, sibling     13a BG / 13b WUR
#   pair 7  health, hard, parent     7a WB / 7b URG        pair 14 home, mixed, parent      14a UG / 14b WBR
#   pair 15 money, mixed, friend    15a WB / 15b URG       pair 17 safety, mixed, parent    17a WU / 17b BRG
#   pair 16 health, mixed, child    16a UR / 16b WBG       pair 18 standing, mixed, sibling 18a RG / 18b WUB

