scene W: Family is not left on the doorstep. Whatever it costs, {N} knows what is right here.
scene U: {N} thinks of the spare room, the bills, how long a little while really is, and what this town offers someone in that trade.
scene B: {Ns} home was built the hard way. A guest with no job and no date to leave is a weight, whatever the love.
scene R: The bag, the smile, the long bus ride without calling first: {N} could laugh and cry at once.
scene G: Kin have always taken each other in when times turn. A shared roof is how families get through.
