- U>R | find them a short course in a trade this town is short of | door | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 62
- B>G | put in a word with your own boss, and get them taken on | v: benevolence, achievement | act: put in a word with their own boss, and get the sibling taken on | chance: 66
- R>W | march them to the job centre today, before they lose heart | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 50
- G>U | ask the old neighbours and relatives here who might need a hand | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 80
works: Within a few months {sibling} has work in {Ns} town, and Sunday dinners have one more chair.
works: {sibling} gets back on their feet, and never forgets who opened the door.
fails: The weeks stretch into months, and the small things about sharing a home start to grate.
fails: Nothing comes up, and {sibling} goes back to {their_town} with the same one bag.

