- G>B | tell them to put the new wages into a house, the old reliable way | v: tradition, security | chance: 50
works: {friend} is touched, and the friendship feels as close as it did years ago.
works: The good news warms {Ns} whole week, and the two of them talk more often after it.
fails: Something in the answer lands wrong, and {friend} goes a little quiet afterwards.
fails: The calls thin out as {friend} gets busy with the new life, and {N} feels left behind.

