times: Losing much of one's savings to a fraud, a failed lender or a sudden jump in costs is rare in any one year but met by many families over a lifetime; older people are the most often targeted by swindles (estimate)
gap: 3-8
scene: {parent} has sounded odd on the phone for weeks, and tonight it comes out: since {far_event} in {their_town}, the money has gone wrong, and the savings put by for old age are mostly gone. {parent} is ashamed, and keeps saying it is nothing, they will manage. They have not told anyone else.
scene W: A parent who raised {N} should not be ashamed to ask {N} for anything. It is {Ns} turn now.
scene U: {N} wants the whole picture: how much, where it went, whether any of it can be got back, and what the monthly budget looks like now.
scene B: {Ns} own savings are not large, and a parent with no cushion could need help for twenty years.
scene R: {N} hates hearing {parent} sound small and ashamed, and is furious at whoever let this happen.
scene G: The family has always said it: children look after the ones who looked after them. That has not changed.
