- W>B | file every claim there is, with the police and the courts | v: security, universalism | chance: 66
- U>R | find the others who lost money too, and start a group to fight back | door | v: universalism, stimulation | chance: 56
- B>G | lend them money against the family house, so it stays in the family | binds | v: power, tradition | chance: 60
- R>W | tell the rest of the family at once, so no one carries it alone | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 82
- G>U | ask the old family friends there what really happened in town | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 74
works: {parent} sleeps again, and the shame turns, slowly, into a story they can tell.
works: Bit by bit the money is put right, and {parent} stops apologising on every call.
fails: Little of the money comes back, and {parent} grows careful and anxious in a way {N} has never seen.
fails: The subject becomes a sore spot, and {parent} hides the next bill.

