scene W: Debts are there to be paid, and a family that hides things ends up with exactly this drawer. Everything has to be put in order.
scene U: The letters are a puzzle: who is owed, at what rate, and which threats are real and which are bluff.
scene B: Whoever pays this debt owns a piece of the problem from now on. {N} would want something solid in return.
scene R: The hurt of being kept out of it hits {N} first, and then a rush of fierce love.
scene G: {parent} grew up in a time and a place where nobody spoke of money troubles. The pride is old, and it runs in the family.
