scene W: Gifts between siblings have their own rules: what is fair, what is owed, and what it will mean at the next family gathering.
scene U: {N} wonders whether {sibling} has thought it through: tax, the years ahead, how fast money like this tends to go.
scene B: A share is a share. {Ns} own plans could use exactly this, and {sibling} is offering.
scene R: The joy in the voice is pure, and {N} is swept up in it, laughing too.
scene G: The two of them grew up with very little. Luck like this, coming back round to the family, feels like the old story turning right.
