scene W: When a town asks someone to serve, {N} thinks that is not a thing to wave away lightly.
scene U: {N} wants to know what the seat really involves: the hours, the meetings, the people already on the board.
scene B: A seat on the board is real say over a whole town. {N} is proud, and a little envious.
scene R: {N} can hear that {sibling} is thrilled and frightened in equal measure, and wants to say whatever {sibling} needs to hear.
scene G: The family has never had anyone on the board. {N} wonders what it would do to the household, and to the old friendships.
- W | tell them it is a duty, and if the town asks they should serve | v: conformity, universalism | chance: 68
- U | help them weigh the hours, the pay and what it costs the household | v: self-direction, security | chance: 82
- B | tell them to take it, because a seat on the board beats a quiet life | v: power, achievement | chance: 70
- R | tell them to say no tonight if their gut says no | v: self-direction, hedonism | chance: 76
- G | tell them to ask their own household first, and abide by what it says | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 74
- W>R | go there for the first meeting and sit in the front row | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 72
- U>G | help them learn what the old families of the town want from the board | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 58
- B>W | tell them to stand only if the board agrees to their terms for the town | v: power, universalism | chance: 70
- R>U | call them back every night that week to talk it through until they know | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 64
- G>B | tell them to take the seat and use it to keep the family business safe | v: security, power | chance: 66
works: Whatever {sibling} decides, it sits right, and the town respects the answer.
works: {sibling} takes the seat and finds the work hard but worth it, and calls {N} after every meeting.
fails: The seat eats every evening, and {sibling} sounds tired and harried on every call.
fails: {sibling} turns it down and spends months wondering, a little sourly, what might have been.
